          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Nobel Prizes</strong><br>\nIn his will, Nobel left the majority of his fortune to establish the Nobel Prizes. These prizes were to be awarded to individuals and organizations that contributed significantly to the fields of physics, chemistry, medicine, literature, and peace. Nobel wanted his legacy to reflect his belief in the betterment of humanity through knowledge and understanding.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Controversies and Criticisms</strong><br>\nNobel's invention of dynamite was controversial because it was used not only for constructive purposes but also in warfare. This led to criticism that Nobel, ironically, had made it easier to take human lives. His establishment of the Nobel Peace Prize is often seen as a way to compensate for the destructive potential of his inventions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Nobel's Last Years and Legacy</strong><br>\nNobel's health declined in his later years, and he passed away in Italy in 1896. His will specified that his fortune was to be used to create the Nobel Prizes, which have become a prestigious international accolade. Nobel's legacy lives on through these awards, which celebrate human achievement and encourage progress and peace.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
